        "revid": 1374526332,
        "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux\" style=\"display:none\">Core software component of every major web browser</div>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1368532237\">.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Not to be confused with <a href=\"/wiki/JavaScript_engine\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"JavaScript engine\">JavaScript engine</a>.</div>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><p>A <b>browser engine</b> (also known as a <b>layout engine</b> or <b>rendering engine</b>) is a core software component of every major <a href=\"/wiki/Web_browser\" title=\"Web browser\">web browser</a>. The primary job of a browser engine is to transform <a href=\"/wiki/HTML\" title=\"HTML\">HTML</a> documents and other resources of a <a href=\"/wiki/Web_page\" title=\"Web page\">web page</a> into an interactive visual representation on a <a href=\"/wiki/User_(computing)\" title=\"User (computing)\">user</a>'s device.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐api‐ext.eqiad.main‐77f8cc8f9b‐ggdbc\nCached time: 20260918181048\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1]\nCPU time usage: 0.098 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.152 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 248/1000000\nRevision size: 484/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 2014/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 748/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 12/100\nExpensive parser function count: 2/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 409/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.053/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage